1
00:00:00,378 --> 00:00:02,708
(Amy:)We're looking good.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:04,814
We are... (giggles)

3
00:00:04,816 --> 00:00:06,486
(Amy:)Better than good.

4
00:00:06,484 --> 00:00:09,954
(Amy:)I mean, look at you.
Your body's bangin'!

5
00:00:09,955 --> 00:00:11,825
Amy!

6
00:00:11,823 --> 00:00:13,123
Don't "Amy" me.

7
00:00:13,124 --> 00:00:14,154
(Amy:)We're always talking
about how hot Penny is.

8
00:00:14,159 --> 00:00:16,489
(Amy:)Come on-- scientist
to scientist,

9
00:00:16,494 --> 00:00:19,964
(Amy:)how big are those
Hadron Colliders?

10
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,330
(Bernadette:)You're embarrassing me.

11
00:00:24,336 --> 00:00:25,466
(Amy:)Oh, don't be embarrassed.

12
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:27,900
(Amy:)I'll show you the divot
in my spine.

13
00:00:27,906 --> 00:00:30,376
(Amy:)What?
No, no, it's okay.
I was born with it.

14
00:00:30,375 --> 00:00:32,505
(Amy:)If you put a double-A
battery in there,

15
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:35,280
(Amy:)it makes my leg kick.

16
00:00:37,582 --> 00:00:38,682
(Leonard:)All right.

17
00:00:38,683 --> 00:00:40,853
(Sheldon:)Oh, this is already better.
There are

18
00:00:40,852 --> 00:00:43,252
(Sheldon:)far fewer distractions in here.

19
00:00:43,254 --> 00:00:44,424
(Raj:)Plus, this is where our minds

20
00:00:44,422 --> 00:00:45,692
(Raj:)are conditioned
to focus on work.

21
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:47,360
(Leonard:)So, I've been thinking
about the hover boards,

22
00:00:47,359 --> 00:00:50,159
(Leonard:)and maybe there's a way
we could use maglev technology.

23
00:00:50,161 --> 00:00:52,831
(Howard:)Or if we could figure out a
way to supercool the materials,

24
00:00:52,831 --> 00:00:54,431
(Howard:)we could utilize
quantum coupling.

25
00:00:54,432 --> 00:00:56,602
(Sheldon:)Well, I wonder
if anyone's tried that.

26
00:00:56,601 --> 00:00:58,101
(Raj:)Go online and look it up.

27
00:00:58,103 --> 00:00:59,633
(Howard:)Oh, I can't argue with him.

